<WovenDocs::Page
  @id="drawer"
  @title="Drawer"
  @subtitle="Native dialog docked to an edge, sliding in over a backdrop and out again."
  @components="Woven::Drawer"
>
  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Overview" @id="overview">
    <p class="woven-doc__intro">
      The drawer is a native dialog with the modal's mechanics (showModal,
      focus trap, scroll lock, Escape as the cancel event). The kit slides
      it in and out; the component stays mounted through the slide out and
      reports
      <code class="wu-code">@onClosed</code>
      afterwards, timed as run-loop tasks so tests can await it. It renders
      the CSS kit
      <code class="wu-code">wu-drawer</code>
      and ends with its own empty
      <code class="wu-code">wu-layer</code>; menus, popovers and tooltips
      inside it resolve that layer through the layer service (nearest open
      dialog), so they stay interactive while the page behind is inert. Use it for edit
      forms beside a list, where the user wants to keep the list in sight.
    </p>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Features" @id="features">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Docks to the inline end, the inline start or the bottom; three widths, wide by default.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Enter and leave transitions with a closed callback after the animation.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Backdrop click and Escape, each switchable; Escape inside a menu or popover stays there.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Header, body and footer slots, or a custom header block.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Placements" @id="placements">
    <p class="woven-note">One drawer instance serves these examples; each button opens it from a different edge. The body holds a dropdown: open it and press Escape, the menu closes and the drawer stays.</p>
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="placement end"
      @note="Slides from the inline end; the default for edit forms and detail panels beside a list."
      @code={{this.code.placementEnd}}
    >
      <Woven::Button @text="Open end drawer" @onClick={{fn this.openDrawer "end" "md"}} data-test-open-drawer-end />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="placement start"
      @note="Slides from the inline start, mirroring a navigation sidebar."
      @code={{this.code.placementStart}}
    >
      <Woven::Button
        @text="Open start drawer"
        @onClick={{fn this.openDrawer "start" "md"}}
        data-test-open-drawer-start
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="placement bottom"
      @note="Rises from the bottom, the sheet pattern on phones."
      @code={{this.code.placementBottom}}
    >
      <Woven::Button
        @text="Open bottom drawer"
        @onClick={{fn this.openDrawer "bottom" "md"}}
        data-test-open-drawer-bottom
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Sizes" @id="sizes">
    {{#each this.sizeExamples as |example|}}
      <WovenDocs::Example @title={{example.title}} @note={{example.note}} @code={{example.code}}>
        <Woven::Button
          @text="Open {{example.size}} drawer"
            @onClick={{fn this.openDrawer "end" example.size}}
          data-test-woven-drawer-size={{example.size}}
        />
      </WovenDocs::Example>
    {{/each}}

    <span class="wu-text sm muted" data-test-woven-drawer-closed>Closed {{this.closedCount}} times (counted after the leave transition).</span>

    <Woven::Drawer
      @open={{this.drawerOpen}}
      @title="Unit filters"
      @placement={{this.drawerPlacement}}
      @size={{this.drawerSize}}
      @onClose={{this.closeDrawer}}
      @onClosed={{this.afterClosed}}
    >
      <:body>
        <Woven::Text @text="Filter units by region, status, and rent range." />
        <Woven::Field @label="Area" @tooltip="Opens in a native popover inside the drawer, above it in the top layer.">
          <Woven::Dropdown
            @options={{this.areaOptions}}
            @value={{this.drawerArea}}
            @onSelect={{this.pickArea}}
            @align="start"
            @placeholder="Any area"
          />
        </Woven::Field>
        <Woven::Popover @title="Rent range">
          <:trigger as |toggle isOpen|>
            <Woven::Button
              @text="Rent help"
                    @onClick={{toggle}}
              aria-expanded={{if isOpen "true" "false"}}
              data-test-woven-drawer-popover
            />
          </:trigger>
          <:body>
            <Woven::Text @size="sm" @text="Escape closes this popover and leaves the drawer open." />
          </:body>
        </Woven::Popover>
      </:body>
      <:footer>
        <Woven::Button @text="Close" @onClick={{this.closeDrawer}} />
      </:footer>
    </Woven::Drawer>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Slots" @id="slots">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Body, footer and onClosed"
      @note="The body holds the form, the footer its actions, and onClosed fires after the slide out so state can reset without flashing. This is the snippet behind the drawer above."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.basic}}
    >
      <Woven::Text
        @size="sm"
        @muted={{true}}
        @text="Open any drawer above, pick an area, close it: the pick resets after the leave transition and the counter increments."
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Header block"
      @note="Replaces the whole header, close button included; put the yielded id on your heading so the dialog keeps its accessible name."
      @code={{this.code.header}}
    >
      <Woven::Button
        @text="Open custom header"
        @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "headerOpen" true}}
        data-test-woven-open-drawer-header
      />
      <Woven::Drawer @open={{this.headerOpen}} @placement="end" @size="sm" @onClose={{fn this.setOpen "headerOpen" false}}>
        <:header as |titleId|>
          <h2 id={{titleId}} class="wu-drawer-title">Custom header</h2>
          <Woven::Tag @variant="info" @text="3 filters" />
        </:header>
        <:body><Woven::Text @text="The heading above carries the yielded id." /></:body>
        <:footer><Woven::Button @text="Close" @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "headerOpen" false}} /></:footer>
      </Woven::Drawer>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Dismissal" @id="dismissal">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Backdrop click ignored"
      @note="closeOnBackdrop false protects a long form from a stray click on the page behind it."
      @code={{this.code.noBackdrop}}
    >
      <Woven::Button
        @text="Open, backdrop locked"
        @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "lockedOpen" true}}
        data-test-woven-open-drawer-locked
      />
      <Woven::Drawer @open={{this.lockedOpen}} @title="Backdrop click ignored" @placement="end" @size="sm" @closeOnBackdrop={{false}} @onClose={{fn this.setOpen "lockedOpen" false}}>
        <:body><Woven::Text @text="Click outside: nothing happens. Escape or the X still close it." /></:body>
        <:footer><Woven::Button @text="Close" @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "lockedOpen" false}} /></:footer>
      </Woven::Drawer>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Escape ignored"
      @note="closeOnEsc false for a drawer that owns an in-progress save; pair it with a disabled close while busy."
      @code={{this.code.noEsc}}
    >
      <Woven::Button
        @text="Open, Escape locked"
        @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "noEscOpen" true}}
        data-test-woven-open-drawer-no-esc
      />
      <Woven::Drawer @open={{this.noEscOpen}} @title="Escape ignored" @placement="end" @size="sm" @closeOnEsc={{false}} @onClose={{fn this.setOpen "noEscOpen" false}}>
        <:body><Woven::Text @text="Press Escape: nothing happens. The X and the backdrop still close it." /></:body>
        <:footer><Woven::Button @text="Close" @onClick={{fn this.setOpen "noEscOpen" false}} /></:footer>
      </Woven::Drawer>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Arguments" @id="arguments">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.argRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Callbacks" @id="callbacks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="callbacks" @rows={{this.callbackRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Blocks" @id="blocks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="blocks" @rows={{this.blockRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Accessibility" @id="accessibility">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>A native dialog opened with showModal(), labeled by the title; the same focus trap, first-control focus and focus restore as the modal.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The browser sends Escape to the topmost dialog only, so a confirm modal opened from inside it takes precedence; Escape inside a menu or popover is canceled there.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The slide is skipped under prefers-reduced-motion, and the leave wait follows the dialog's own transition time.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="RTL" @id="rtl">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>start and end are logical edges; the kit mirrors the slide under dir="rtl", so the panel always enters from its own edge.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>
</WovenDocs::Page>
